        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix compaction fallback for OpenAI Responses auth",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #98814.\n\nOpenAI Responses auth already skips incompatible OAuth profiles while walking normal auth order, but compaction can pass the current session profile as an explicit `profileId`. For long direct sessions that inherited an OpenAI OAuth profile, this made `openai/openai-responses` throw before it could reach an API-key backup.\n\nThis PR now:\n\n- adds an opt-in `fallbackOnIncompatibleProfile` resolver flag\n- threads `authProfileIdSource` through embedded, manual/native, and harness compaction\n- enables incompatible-profile fallback only for explicitly auto/inherited profiles\n- keeps user-selected and missing/unknown-source profiles locked and fail-fast\n- preserves profile source only while compaction stays on the same provider\n- refreshes the branch onto upstream `main` at `ff1c29eaf903`\n\nDefault explicit-profile behavior remains fail-fast outside this narrowly gated compaction path.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nLong-running direct sessions can hit transcript compaction while using `openai/gpt-5.5` through an inherited OAuth profile. The compaction runtime then calls the OpenAI Responses API, which requires API-key auth. Auto/inherited profiles may now fall through to the configured API-key backup, while explicit user locks are never silently replaced.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExisting reporter proof is unchanged: live logs from a direct Signal session showed `compactionTokens=272001` followed by `Auth profile ... uses oauth auth, but openai/openai-responses requires an OpenAI API key profile.` After applying the local installed-dist patch through Hook 50 and restarting OpenClaw, `openclaw status` reported the gateway reachable and the session recovered to roughly `113k/272k` tokens.\n\n## Regression Coverage Added\n\n- resolver fallback from incompatible OAuth to API-key auth order\n- default explicit-profile fail-fast behavior\n- locked-profile fail-fast behavior even when fallback is requested\n- auto vs. user vs. unknown compaction source policy\n- source preservation on same-provider compaction and removal on provider switch\n- direct compaction credential-lookup arguments for auto, user, and missing sources\n\n## Validation\n\nHistorical validation performed before the original PR was opened:\n\n- `CI=true pnpm exec vitest run src/agents/model-auth.test.ts`\n- `CI=true pnpm exec vitest run src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/compaction-runtime-context.test.ts`\n- `CI=true pnpm tsgo:core`\n- `CI=true pnpm tsgo:core:test`\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/agents/model-auth.ts src/agents/model-auth.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/compact.ts src/agents/harness/compaction.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe refreshed head and new source-gating tests were not run locally in the connector-only repair environment. GitHub CI is the validation source for commit `2729a45e5048`.\n",
        "branch": "codex/compaction-openai-responses-api-key",
